<title>NEW ZEALAND: FCL Energy 1st half profit up sharply.</title>
<headline>FCL Energy 1st half profit up sharply.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1996-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr to Dec 31, 1996.</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				   126 vs 20</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 35.2 vs 3.7</p>
<p>    Div (cents)				  8.5 vs n/a</p>
<p>    Turnover				     493 vs 417</p>
<p>    Pretax profit				142 vs 15</p>
<p>    Tax				   debit (17) vs credit 2.0</p>
<p>Dividend carries 4.19 cps imputation credit.</p>
<p>Pay date April 2</p>
<p>Reg date March 14</p>
<p>    Ex div   March 17</p>
<p>Note - Fletcher Energy is the energy division of Fletcher Challenge. Market expectations were for a net profit before abnormal items of just under NZ$100 million. FCL Energy made a NZ$32 million abnormal gain from the sale of its stake in Bay of Plenty Electricity. Net profit included NZ$8.0 million in depreciation and NZ$121 million in depletions.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
</text>
